                <pb facs="0513" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/268: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McCafferty</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1934-03-05T20:20:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1934-03-04T16:00:00-06:00">undated</date>].<lb/>[Received
                        March 5—8:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. The following telegram has been sent to Managua: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 4, 4 p.m. Your March 3. The Foreign Office informs me that the
                            membership of the Salvadoran delegation has not yet been decided upon
                            but that this [<hi rendition="#italic">they?</hi>] will advise me
                            immediately upon their appointment. Repeated to Central American
                            missions.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McCafferty</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
